Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
CODE DOCUMENTATION

File: Theory/OL/Open-loop-AND.nb
Paper: An information-theoretic perspective on feed-forward loop abundances \
in transcriptional networks
Authors: Mintu Nandi, Sudip Chattopadhyay, and Suman K Banik
Contact: mintunandi@ubi.s.u-tokyo.ac.jp; sudip@chem.iiests.ac.in; \
skbanik@jcbose.ac.in

Purpose
Evaluates the open-loop reference for all motifs and both organisms under the \
AND gate and calculates the joint information I(X, X_tilde; Z).

How to run
Open the notebook in Wolfram Mathematica and evaluate the input cells.

Inputs and outputs
No external input files are required. Parameter values and analytical \
expressions are embedded in the notebook. Results are returned as evaluated \
cells, printed tables, and plots.

Code-to-manuscript notation
x1 -> X, the direct-path input; x2 -> X_tilde, the independent input to the \
indirect path; x1av, x2av, yav, zav -> <x>, <x_tilde>, <y>, <z>; Kx1z, Kx2y, \
Kyz -> K_XZ, K_XY, K_YZ; vx1z, vx2z -> covariances of X and X_tilde with Z; \
vzcx1x2 -> sigma_Z|X,X_tilde^2; Ix1x2z -> I(X,X_tilde;Z) = I_path(X;Z).\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9962825003528976`*^9},
 Background->GrayLevel[
  0.95],ExpressionUUID->"4f136a87-d6bb-be4b-940c-61484f865e79"],

